=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
title: A genuinely unreadable production file is opaque evidence, refused for a weakened assertion (D-199)
d199: D-199 (0.12) refuses repair evidence for this rule. The inputs are unchanged; they were the case runner_opaque_native_neg, held at warn by that evidence. REPAIR_EVIDENCE_REFUSED pins that the production change still reached the finding.
origin: FP guard — the 2026-08-11 widening must not turn every unreadable prod change into a block; since D-199 the guard is the label REPAIR_EVIDENCE_REFUSED (the file still counts as opaque production), not the verdict
=== before: src/core.rs ===
pub fn invoice_total(items: &[f64], tax: f64) -> f64 {
    items.iter().sum::<f64>()
}
=== after: src/core.rs ===
pub fn invoice_total(items: &[f64], tax: f64) -> f64 {
    items.iter().sum::<f64>() * (1.0 + tax)
}
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) == 105.0
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) > 0
